<article-title>Sources of diagnostic error in fine needle aspiration of the thyroid</article-title><source>Cancer</source><year>1989</year><volume>63</volume><fpage>718</fpage><lpage>725</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2914278</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B24"><label>24</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ahuja</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Ng</surname><given-names>CF</given-names></name><name><surname>King</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Metreweli</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Solitary cystic nodal metastasis from occult papillary carcinoma of the thyroid mimicking a branchial cyst: a potential pitfall</article-title><source>Clin Radiol</source><year>1998</year><volume>53</volume><fpage>61</fpage><lpage>63</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9464439</pub-id></element-citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-group><fig id="F1" position="float"><label>Fig. 1</label><caption><p>52-year-old man with recurrent papillary thyroid carcinoma.</p></caption><p>US (transverse view) shows heterogeneous and hyperechoic elongated lymph node (arrow) with focal cystic change (arrowhead) in left lateral neck (level IV). Maximal and minimal diameters were 9 mm and 4 mm, respectively. Result of US-fine-needle aspiration biopsy cytology was suboptimal (mainly blood), but measured Thyroglobulin from aspirate of node was 2,640 ng/ml.</p><graphic xlink:href="kjr-10-106-g001"/></fig><table-wrap id="T1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>FNAB-Tg, FNAB-Cytology, FNAB-Tg/Cytology, and Surgical Pathology Results for 76 Cervical Lymph Nodes</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjr-10-106-i001"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>Note.-FNAB = fine-needle aspiration biopsy, Tg = thyroglobulin</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T2" position="float"><label>Table 2</label><caption><p>Diagnostic Accuracies of FNAB-Tg, FNAB-Cytology, and Combined FNAB-Tg/Cytology</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjr-10-106-i002"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>Note.-FNAB = fine-needle aspiration biopsy, Tg = thyroglobulin, PPV = positive predictive value, NPV = negative predictive value, FNAB-Tg/cytology = combined results of FNAB-Tg and FNAB-cytology.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T3" position="float"><label>Table 3</label><caption><p>Statistical Analysis for Assessment of Cervical Node Metastasis by FNAB-Tg, FNAB-Cytology, and Combined FNAB-Tg/Cytology</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjr-10-106-i003"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>Note.-FNAB = fine-needle aspiration biopsy, Tg = thyroglobulin</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T4" position="float"><label>Table 4</label><caption><p>US Features of 76 Cervical Lymph Nodes</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjr-10-106-i004"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>Note.-L/T = longitudinal/transverse diameter ratio</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T5" position="float"><label>Table 5</label><caption><p>Cases of FNAB-Tg Benefit and Corresponding US Features</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjr-10-106-i005"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>Note.-FNAB = fine-needle aspiration biopsy, Tg = thyroglobulin, L/T = longitudinal/transverse diameter ratio</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-group></article>